the 28th annual summerlin council  patriotic parade rolled out today to  celebrate our nation's independence day  hundreds gathered along the parade route  to see more than 20 giant inflatable  balloons and over 70 floats christian  casares shows us some of the excitement  a sea of red white and blue along  village center circle in summerland as  an annual tradition continued on this  fourth of july the music was fun and my  favorite part was a marching band this  year the summerlin council patriotic  parade was back after the pandemic  paused the celebration honoring our  military and keeping the las vegas  spirit alive so awesome this is so well  needed it's so great to see everybody  together again not wearing masks we can  see their faces and the whole community  coming together  more than 70 floats made their way from  hill center drive and hill point road  around village center circle to spring  gate lane our very own brian loftus and  sherry swanks on the mic as a parade  strolled by the reason that the  summerlin parade initially came together  as kind of a grassroots effort in the in  95 and we certainly are proud to carry  on that tradition  las vegas now mercedes martinez and jc  fernandez also hosting the parade while  more than 50 thousand people cheered the  palo verde high school marching band and  the nevada latino arts and culture  association among others it's very  special all parts of the community are  represented and it makes you happy to  live here 25 giant balloons colorful  floats and even lady liberty kept the  crowd smiling as hundreds of american  flags waving along the parade route i  just loved all the beautiful music and  all the beautiful floats and everybody  was nice christian casa is live local  now  the parade is organized by the summerlin  council about 2500 people were in  today's parade more than 500 local  volunteers helping putting it all  together again
 

